        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "To a solution of H2salen (0.268 g, 1 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (4 mL) was slowly added Sm(acac)3·H2O (0.225 g, 0.5 mmol) and Eu(acac)3·H2O (0.225 g, 0.5 mmol) in MeOH (5 mL) at room temperature. A yellow precipitate formed immediately. After stirring for 3 h the solution became bright yellow. Crystals suitable for X-ray determination were obtained by slow diffusion of ethyl ether into the solution at room temperature for one week, as for 3. ICP showed Sm:Eu = 1.96:1.91 (50.6% Sm of total metal).",
