        "summary": "Solid-state dual SmIII/EuIII emission at room temperature. Eu bands at 580, 593 and 613 nm are stronger than in homometallic 4, while Sm emission near 645 nm is partly quenched versus 3. Lifetimes: Sm 18±1 μs; Eu 114±2 μs (vs 179±1 μs in 4). Quantum yield 1% (vs 5±1% for 4). Authors conclude no productive Sm→Eu energy transfer in 1.",
